diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 058eba9..6708dd1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -120 +120 @@ eth-genesis-state-generator beaconchain \
-- Validators from mnemonics get their keys from the signing secret key `sk`, the EIP-2333 key at `m/12381/3600/<index>/0/0`, so a client holding the usual validator keystore can derive them. The leanXMSS seed is `sha256("leanxmss-seed" || sk)`. The VRF tree has depth 31; with `vrf_seed = sha256("vrf-seed" || sk)`, leaf `i` is `sha256(vrf_seed || uint64_le(i))` for `i < 2**20` and 32 zero bytes above, which keeps the tree cheap to build and covers the first 2**20 slots.
+- Validators from mnemonics get their keys from the signing secret key `sk`, the EIP-2333 key at `m/12381/3600/<index>/0/0`, so a client holding the usual validator keystore can derive them. The leanXMSS seed is `sha256("leanxmss-seed" || sk)`. The VRF tree has depth 31; with `vrf_seed = sha256("vrf-seed" || sk)`, leaf `i` is `keccak256(vrf_seed || uint64_le(i))` for `i < 2**20` and 32 zero bytes above, which keeps the tree cheap to build and covers the first 2**20 slots. Internal nodes use Keccak-256 over the left and right child.
@@ -122 +122 @@ eth-genesis-state-generator beaconchain \
-- Deriving a key and its VRF root takes a few CPU seconds. `--xmss-pubkey-cache <dir>` stores them in `<dir>/<mnemonic fingerprint>.bin`, where the record of index `i` is the 64 bytes at offset `64*i` (public key, then VRF root) and the fingerprint is the first 8 bytes of `sha256("leanxmss-vrf-keys" || BIP-39 seed)`, in hex. `--xmss-pubkey-url <base url>` fetches the needed range of the same file from a remote location before deriving what is still missing.
+- Deriving a key and its VRF root takes a few CPU seconds. `--xmss-pubkey-cache <dir>` stores them in `<dir>/<mnemonic fingerprint>.bin`, where the record of index `i` is the 64 bytes at offset `64*i` (public key, then VRF root) and the fingerprint is the first 8 bytes of `sha256("leanxmss-padded-keccak-vrf-keys" || BIP-39 seed)`, in hex. `--xmss-pubkey-url <base url>` fetches the needed range of the same file from a remote location before deriving what is still missing.
